* se-receiver-dp-pex -- sky130 single-ended D+ receiver thresholds, post-layout (klt pex)
*
* Post-layout counterpart of sim/se-receiver-dp-thresholds: identical circuit body, measurements and
* checks. The single .include below names the schematic-leg DUT shim (se_receiver_dp_pex_dut.spice:
* design/netlist/se_receiver_dp.spice with its .subckt declaration line reordered to the
* extracted header's pin order) -- the swap point klt pex re-points at the extracted
* netlist for the extracted-side leg. Every DUT instance line's nets are written in
* that same order, so one positional instance line serves both legs with the same
* net-to-pin mapping. The request supplies the .lib corner section, .temp and the
* supply sweep (vsup).
*
* Stimulus (unchanged from the committed bench): one DC sweep of the line input DP
* from 0 V to 3.0 V in 1 mV steps (3001 points), ideal source. 3.0 V is the lowest
* matrix supply, so the input never exceeds the receiver's own rail.


.include "se_receiver_dp_pex_dut.spice"

vsup vdd 0 dc 3.3
vi vdd vddr dc 0
vin in 0 dc 0
ehalf half 0 vol='v(vdd)/2'
xrx in rxdp vddr 0 se_receiver_dp
